{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","file--1","process--1","instance--984a6f68-81a0-5159-abef-0268d29adcf7","file--2","instance--faafbd18-4dd4-5506-9061-a39651fa8632","file--3","directory--1","file--4","instance--c9ac7d3e-0e27-5d69-82d2-4ace9f351fe7","instance--2e7f7375-ee60-55ba-a81c-c3596ee30290","instance--d8016d87-9bd1-5636-9af6-dcb2ce5eebc2","instance--e831865a-75df-5bd8-80c8-84a120da94d2","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--5c474795-7a46-5c6c-af4d-203928d704a3","instance--c7fe5a56-7368-5f6f-817b-9af826352b09","instance--871aff85-c69f-5bfe-96c0-624f87121fe2","instance--669e2d27-86a1-5407-b925-c3cfee206b81","instance--0dfafbfd-0f45-564f-ad54-9ef5e5327ecc","instance--da58edb7-8677-5e51-a685-3c1834f88447","instance--f62b03fe-bbd9-58e6-a0e7-2dd2387ae128","instance--9065a7c9-ce5d-5e80-b152-07d24308602d","instance--7ac03378-cee4-56b0-806f-6a8043dc47b9","instance--3768496b-a6ee-5827-8f05-363ce28e5e1d","instance--db9bfccd-b016-5bea-a415-ab12047197d6","instance--466bc914-7c14-51e8-81ad-8b36cf13e996"],"properties":[["name","Silence malicious CHM execution flow"],["description","Article describing two Silence APT campaigns using malicious CHM files that execute scripts to download and run VBScript stages."],["scope","campaign"],["author",[["name","Igor Mikhaylov"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","web.archive.org"],["url","https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https:/cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Open CHM and create scheduled task"],["description","So, once the victim opens the file, the script inside uses schtasks.exe to create a task with the name \u201c4\u201d, which downloads and runs \u201cmnms\u201d from 146.0.77[.]104, then the task is deleted."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1053.005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Download and run mnms VBScript"],["description","So, once the victim opens the file, the script inside uses schtasks.exe to create a task with the name \u201c4\u201d, which downloads and runs \u201cmnms\u201d from 146.0.77[.]104, then the task is deleted. What\u2019s \u201cmnms\u201d? It\u2019s a VB script, which will download the next stage."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Copy cmd.exe to dmw.exe"],["description","This time there is no tasks, but still something interesting. Once opened by the victim, the script inside the CHM file will copy cmd.exe to %APPDATA% as dmw.exe, then it uses it to download and run \u201crogr.php\u201d from 185.70.186[.]146."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1036.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Download and run rogr.php VBScript"],["description","This time there is no tasks, but still something interesting. Once opened by the victim, the script inside the CHM file will copy cmd.exe to %APPDATA% as dmw.exe, then it uses it to download and run \u201crogr.php\u201d from 185.70.186[.]146. Again, \u201crogr.php\u201d is a VB script, which will download the next stage."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--8cf549a5-7e7d-51cf-9368-9b5e0744592a","120":"instance--06d4fda8-e0bf-574e-b3d8-a62c44712794","150":"instance--bb5815b3-6a43-5e3f-b9bc-9862b25fcfbb","180":"instance--f044d6bc-5582-5c4b-8062-d78469e24a48","210":"instance--e728313e-5605-515c-b37b-9ffb6e4816de","240":"instance--2e67ae43-8ff1-546b-b53a-2147995d4ec2","270":"instance--9f6cbb4c-d86c-53ed-890d-a560dca0b584","30":"instance--3bed1646-ea3a-5567-b439-b19993f3bb89","300":"instance--eaaf034a-e88c-5110-84f3-b644fd9af752","330":"instance--1f54afc1-8d53-569a-9f5a-625de523f9b0","60":"instance--e5c6eb85-2474-59e2-b136-a99f7e8c85a3","90":"instance--f4164786-5d40-5ba5-9ff1-764895cce7f5"},"id":"file","instance":"file--1","properties":[["value","Maket dizayna debitovoy korp karty.CHM"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"citation":null,"excerpt":"Maket dizayna debitovoy korp karty.CHM (Debit corporate card design template)","source":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220119133748/https:/cyberforensicator.com/2019/01/20/silence-dissecting-malicious-chm-files-and-performing-forensic-analysis/","source_field":"normalized_text","source_object_id":null}]]],["display_name","Maket dizayna debitovoy korp karty.CHM"],["name","Maket dizayna debitovoy korp karty.CHM"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4e942bfd-4264-555c-8748-7eb2e999ff13","120":"instance--f044726d-ee55-52f4-88b4-fd39ff2b8e8d","150":"instance--14187d6c-2f13-51e8-bde1-91e065756a74","180":"instance--72fbf7a0-91d0-5e9f-b83b-7f5b189a8cef","210":"instance--e1937ddc-1102-52c0-9709-5f7600aba57e","240":"instance--a15e1468-8c2f-564d-98f3-27d39b4d492e","270":"instance--7f152962-47bb-5430-9fc9-64786b99deff","30":"instance--b1dba1f2-201d-5b13-abad-98f28b800a58","300":"instance--eeb12b43-767c-5026-84e8-5841c4408405","330":"instance--b6b5fa0e-b8a7-5f